---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/home/SiteFooter.astro';
import { paths, lessonCount, videoLessonCount } from '../lib/academy';

/*
 * The Academy: the curriculum as a set of learning paths, following api-portal's
 * and arch-portal's academy pages so the three hubs teach in the same shape —
 * kicker, promise, honest "in preparation" notice, then one card per path with
 * its lessons and a pointer to what is readable today.
 *
 * Published before the lessons exist on purpose. A curriculum is a commitment
 * about what is worth learning and in what order, and that is worth reviewing
 * early; "coming soon" on its own tells a reader nothing.
 *
 * Deliberately not the Hero component: this is a second-level page in the same
 * family as the other hubs' /academy, and it uses that page's lighter header
 * rather than the full-bleed banner /catalog gets.
 */
---

<Layout
	title="Academy — Dev Hub"
	description="Seven learning paths through effective software development: connected development, UX-first, test-first, contract-first, patterns-oriented design, software craftsmanship, and semi-automation with AI."
>
	<main id="main" class="mx-auto w-full max-w-5xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-20">
		<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="text-sm">
			<a href="/" class="text-ink-muted underline-offset-4 hover:text-brand hover:underline dark:text-slate-400 dark:hover:text-sky-400">
				Home
			</a>
			<span aria-hidden="true" class="mx-2 text-ink-muted dark:text-slate-500">/</span>
			<span class="text-ink-muted dark:text-slate-400">Academy</span>
		</nav>

		<p class="mt-6 text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.16em] text-brand uppercase dark:text-sky-400">
			Learning paths
		</p>
		<h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-4xl">
			The hub holds the practices. The Academy teaches you why each one is there.
		</h1>
		<p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-base text-ink-muted sm:text-lg dark:text-slate-400">
			Seven paths through effective software development, in the order the argument runs:
			connect the specialists, start from the user, let the tests drive the design, make the
			boundaries explicit, learn the pattern vocabulary, question every line — and only then
			hand work to a machine.
		</p>

		<!--
			Amber rather than the brand colour: this is a caveat, not a feature, and
			it should read as one on first glance.
		-->
		<p class="mt-8 rounded-xl border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 p-5 text-sm dark:border-amber-700/60 dark:bg-amber-950/40">
			<strong>In preparation.</strong>
			<span class="mt-1 block text-ink-muted dark:text-slate-400">
				The curriculum below is settled; the lessons are still being written, and there is
				nothing to enrol in yet. Every path links to the documentation that covers its
				ground today.
			</span>
		</p>

		<section aria-labelledby="format" class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-7 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-night-raised">
			<h2 id="format" class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Told as stories</h2>
			<p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-ink-muted dark:text-slate-400">
				Development practice is taught badly as a list of definitions and well as a sequence
				of decisions someone had to live with. So the lessons carrying a
				<span class="mx-1 inline-flex items-center gap-1 align-middle text-brand dark:text-sky-400">
					<svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="inline h-4 w-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
						<circle cx="10" cy="10" r="7.5" />
						<path d="M8.5 7.5 13 10l-4.5 2.5V7.5Z" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" />
					</svg>
					<span class="font-semibold">story</span>
				</span>
				mark come with a short video in narrative form: a team with a problem, the option
				they took, what it bought them and what it cost. {videoLessonCount} of the
				{lessonCount} lessons are planned that way — the rest are short enough to read.
			</p>
		</section>

		<h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">The curriculum</h2>
		<ul class="mt-6 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
			{
				paths.map((path) => (
					<li class="flex h-full flex-col rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-7 shadow-sm dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-night-raised">
						<span class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
							<span class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.14em] text-brand uppercase dark:text-sky-400">
								{path.level}
							</span>
							<span class="rounded-full bg-slate-100 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide text-ink-muted uppercase dark:bg-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
								Coming soon
							</span>
						</span>

						<h3 class="mt-4 text-xl font-semibold">{path.title}</h3>
						<p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted dark:text-slate-400">{path.summary}</p>

						<ul class="mt-5 grow space-y-2 text-sm text-ink-muted dark:text-slate-400">
							{path.lessons.map((lesson) => (
								<li class="flex gap-3">
									<span
										aria-hidden="true"
										class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand dark:bg-sky-400"
									/>
									<span>
										{lesson.title}
										{lesson.video && (
											<>
												{' '}
												<span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 align-middle text-brand dark:text-sky-400">
													<svg
														viewBox="0 0 20 20"
														class="inline h-3.5 w-3.5"
														fill="none"
														stroke="currentColor"
														stroke-width="2"
														aria-hidden="true"
													>
														<circle cx="10" cy="10" r="7.5" />
														<path d="M8.5 7.5 13 10l-4.5 2.5V7.5Z" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" />
													</svg>
													<span class="sr-only">Includes a storytelling video</span>
												</span>
											</>
										)}
									</span>
								</li>
							))}
						</ul>

						<p class="mt-6 border-t border-slate-200 pt-4 text-sm dark:border-slate-700">
							<span class="text-ink-muted dark:text-slate-400">Read today: </span>
							<a
								href={path.readToday.href}
								class="font-semibold text-brand underline-offset-4 hover:underline dark:text-sky-400"
							>
								{path.readToday.label}
							</a>
						</p>
					</li>
				))
			}
		</ul>

		<section
			aria-labelledby="start-now"
			class="mt-14 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-8 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-night-raised"
		>
			<h2 id="start-now" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">You do not have to wait</h2>
			<p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-ink-muted dark:text-slate-400">
				Every practice the first lessons will teach is already written down, and the fastest
				way to see how they fit together is to pick one team ritual and run it this week.
			</p>
			<div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
				<a
					href="/doc/practices/"
					class="rounded-full bg-brand px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-brand-strong focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-3 focus-visible:outline-brand"
				>
					Read the practices
				</a>
				<a
					href="/doc/code-design/"
					class="rounded-full border border-slate-300 px-6 py-3 font-semibold transition hover:bg-white dark:border-slate-600 dark:hover:bg-night"
				>
					Read the patterns
				</a>
				<a
					href="/catalog"
					class="rounded-full border border-slate-300 px-6 py-3 font-semibold transition hover:bg-white dark:border-slate-600 dark:hover:bg-night"
				>
					Browse the catalogs
				</a>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
	<SiteFooter />
</Layout>
